        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63475,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A few cases have been reported in the broad ligament {6703196; 16196528; 20403052}; ependymoma also occurs in the mesovarium, uterosacral ligament, and pelvis {26107559}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63476,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a pelvic mass and/or pain. Serum CA125 may be elevated {6703196; 16196528; 20403052}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63477,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The patient age range is 13&ndash;45&nbsp;years (median: 24.5&nbsp;years) {6703196; 16196528; 20403052}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63478,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63479,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63480,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are cystic/multicystic or solid, and they range in size from 7 to 14&nbsp;cm {6703196; 16196528; 20403052}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63481,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour cells are columnar/cuboidal, with eosinophilic cytoplasm. Atypia is mild/moderate and the mitotic count is usually low. There is a combination of architectural patterns&nbsp;&ndash; cystic, microcystic, cribriform, papillary, and solid. Ependymal pseudorosettes are seen. Spindle/flattened cells, cilia, ependymal rosettes/canals, cartilage, psammoma bodies, extracellular mucin, eosinophilic material, and myxoid areas may be present. This tumour is positive for GFAP, ER, PR, CK18, CK7, S100, and WT1 and variably positive for CD99 {18360284}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63482,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:45:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
